      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Glatfelter Company operated one of the world’s largest paper mills in Yorklyn for more than a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/pennsylvania_yorklyn",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Yorklyn sits near Brandywine Creek, where historic mills and scenic landscapes still echo the town’s early industrial past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/pennsylvania_yorklyn",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town serves as a gateway to First State National Historical Park, offering trails that showcase Pennsylvania’s colonial heritage.",
